# XrmToolBox / Microsoft Dataverse public client auth POC
#
# Purpose:
# - Verify that the shared Microsoft Dataverse/XrmToolBox public client ID can
#   acquire a delegated token for a specific Dataverse environment.
# - Verify the token by calling Dataverse WhoAmI.
#
# Requirements:
# - VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
# - A user with access to the target Dataverse environment
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Use an environment URL without a trailing slash.
# - This POC uses the OAuth 2.0 device code flow so no client secret is needed.
# - If the shared client is not enabled for device-code flow in your tenant,
#   the first request will fail. In that case we should test interactive
#   authorization-code + PKCE with MSAL instead.

@tenant = organizations
@environmentUrl = https://org8ffb6d07.crm.dynamics.com
@clientId = 51f81489-12ee-4a9e-aaae-a2591f45987d

### 1. Request a device code
# @name deviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenant}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{environmentUrl}}/user_impersonation%20openid%20profile%20offline_access

### 2. Sign in
#
# Run request 1, then open the verification_uri from the response and enter
# the user_code.
#
# Complete sign-in with a user that has access to the Dataverse environment.
#
# Do not run request 3 until sign-in has completed.

### 3. Exchange the device code for a Dataverse access token
# @name token
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenant}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:device_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{deviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

### 4. Verify the token against Dataverse
# A 200 response proves that the token is valid for this Dataverse resource.
# @name whoami
GET {{environmentUrl}}/api/data/v9.2/WhoAmI
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0

### 5. Optional: query a few accounts
GET {{environmentUrl}}/api/data/v9.2/accounts?$select=accountid,name&$top=3
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-MaxVersion: 4.0
OData-Version: 4.0
